Doing this, of course, causes the classic AB-BA deadlock! Because the module (it’s kernel thread (kthread)
1, actually) ignored the lock ordering rule (which we will do in our upcoming demo module when
the module parameter lock_ooo is set to 1; ooo = out-of-order), it deadlocks.
Here’s portions of the relevant code (we again don’t show the whole program here, as we definitely
expect you to clone this book’s GitHub repository, carefully read the code, and try it out yourself):
